@startuml

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFF88
  BorderColor black
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFE0E0
  BorderColor #FF8080
  condition note_Threat
}

actor Alice
actor Bob
actor Charlie
actor Auditor
participant Notary as "Non-Validating Notary"

== 🔄 Identity Setup ==
Bob -> Alice : RequestKeyFlow
note over Bob, Alice
Bob requests confidential identity  
Alice returns a signed challenge response  
Bob maps Alice’s PublicKey → CordaX500Name  
Stored locally in Bob’s IdentityService
end note

== 💼 Optional: Bob’s Account Key ==
note over Bob
Bob uses internal KeyManagementService  
→ freshKey(UUID) for account identity  
→ maps PublicKey → externalId (UUID)
end note

== 💸 Alice Pays Token to Bob ==
note over Alice, Bob
Alice builds a transaction:  
Spends token owned by her conf. identity  
Creates output to Bob’s conf. identity
end note

Alice -> Bob : SyncKeyMappingsFlow
note over Alice, Bob
Alice shares: PublicKey → CordaX500Name  
Bob can now validate input state ownership
end note

Bob -> Alice : SignTransactionFlow
note over Bob, Alice
Bob signs using his conf. key  
→ Indicates acceptance of inputs/outputs  
→ Ensures trustless collaboration
end note

Alice -> Notary : Submit signed transaction (with input hashes)
note over Notary
Non-validating notary:  
Sees only input hashes  
No identity mappings
end note
Notary --> Alice : OK

== 🩸 Threat: Alice Refuses to Share Mappings ==
alt Mapping omitted
note over Bob <<note_Threat>>
Bob cannot validate Alice’s input states  
→ Refuses to sign transaction  
→ Causes soft denial-of-service
end note
else Mapping shared
note over Bob
Bob validates backchain  
→ Signs using conf. key  
→ Transaction proceeds
end note
end alt

== 💸 Bob Pays Token to Charlie ==
note over Bob, Charlie
Bob builds new transaction:  
Spends received token  
Outputs to Charlie's conf. identity
end note

Bob -> Charlie : SyncKeyMappingsFlow
note over Bob, Charlie
Bob shares his PublicKey → CordaX500Name  
Charlie can validate Bob’s input state  
→ But NOT Alice's unless Bob includes it
end note

Charlie -> Bob : SignTransactionFlow
note over Charlie, Bob
Charlie signs using conf. key  
→ Accepts token state  
→ Validates sender (Bob), but not full backchain
end note

Bob -> Notary : Submit signed transaction
Notary --> Bob : OK

== 🧠 Functional Requirement: Backchain Validation ==
note over Charlie
Charlie must validate token backchain  
→ Sees Bob’s conf. key + mapping  
→ Can trust state origin and ownership  
→ Does NOT learn Alice's identity
end note

== 🩸 Threat: Hidden Originator Identity ==
note over Charlie <<note_Threat>>
Alice’s identity not mapped  
→ Charlie cannot validate full history  
→ Privacy preserved, verification limited
end note

== 🛡️ Auditor Node Resolution ==
Charlie -> Auditor : SyncKeyMappingsFlow
note over Auditor
Auditor receives all mappings  
→ Verifies Alice → Bob → Charlie token path  
→ Enables full compliance without public exposure
end note

@enduml
